ul.li:
Verify as_signature on each delegation record using the
signing key of the AS that issued that record (which may differ
across records);

AS Signature (MUST): Confirms the
delegation was authorized by the AS and the record has not
been tampered with;

DIDs (did:): Resolve the DID Document and
check for revocation indicators (e.g., deactivated DID,
rotated verification keys);

The AS enforcing a freshness window on the
delegation_timestamp (see
) — requests
with timestamps outside the acceptable skew (RECOMMENDED:
5 minutes) MUST be rejected;

Sender-constrained tokens (DPoP or mTLS) bind the
token to the legitimate delegatee's key material,
preventing use by a different party;

Token introspection () enables
the Resource Server to check the token's revocation
status in real time;

